241 0 obj
<< /A 590 0 R /ActualText (Diagram illustrating the interaction between users and the Dimensions webapp instance via API endpoints. Users authenticate through `/api/auth.json`, receiving a token. They access various API endpoints for data services, including current and new versions `/api/dsl/v1` and `/api/dsl/v2`. The API instance handles authentication, throttling, and processes JSON queries. API V1 interfaces with services like Solr, Term Extraction, and others through a firewall, while API V2 logs data to Google Cloud services including BigQuery, Logging, and Data Studio.\r\n) /Alt (Diagram illustrating the interaction between users and the Dimensions webapp instance via API endpoints. Users authenticate through `/api/auth.json`, receiving a token. They access various API endpoints for data services, including current and new versions `/api/dsl/v1` and `/api/dsl/v2`. The API instance handles authentication, throttling, and processes JSON queries. API V1 interfaces with services like Solr, Term Extraction, and others through a firewall, while API V2 logs data to Google Cloud services including BigQuery, Logging, and Data Studio.\r\n) /K 0 /P 103 0 R /Pg 233 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
242 0 obj
<< /A 591 0 R /ActualText (Diagram illustrating data sources and their relationships. Categories include Source Titles \(Reports\), Datasets, Policy Documents, Patents, Clinical Trials, Grants, and Publications. Connections highlight links via source titles, publication IDs, clinical trial IDs, and associated or supporting grant IDs.\r\n) /Alt (Diagram illustrating data sources and their relationships. Categories include Source Titles \(Reports\), Datasets, Policy Documents, Patents, Clinical Trials, Grants, and Publications. Connections highlight links via source titles, publication IDs, clinical trial IDs, and associated or supporting grant IDs.\r\n) /K 0 /P 103 0 R /Pg 234 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
243 0 obj
<< /A 592 0 R /ActualText (Flowchart illustrating relationships between researchers, organizations, and various source titles like datasets, publications, grants, patents, clinical trials, reports, and policy documents. Arrows connect these titles to researchers and organizations, showing how they interact and exchange information.\r\n) /Alt (Flowchart illustrating relationships between researchers, organizations, and various source titles like datasets, publications, grants, patents, clinical trials, reports, and policy documents. Arrows connect these titles to researchers and organizations, showing how they interact and exchange information.\r\n) /K 0 /P 103 0 R /Pg 235 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
